<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Lab Tour | Web IR NLP Group @ NUS</title><link>https://wing.comp.nus.edu.sg/tag/lab-tour/</link><atom:link href="https://wing.comp.nus.edu.sg/tag/lab-tour/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><description>Lab Tour</description><generator>Hugo Blox Builder (https://hugoblox.com)</generator><language>en-us</language><lastBuildDate>Fri, 23 Jan 2026 00:00:00 +0000</lastBuildDate><image><url>https://wing.comp.nus.edu.sg/media/icon_hu_ce731d16d7c8719.png</url><title>Lab Tour</title><link>https://wing.comp.nus.edu.sg/tag/lab-tour/</link></image><item><title>WING Hosts a Lab Tour for AAAI 2026 Participants</title><link>https://wing.comp.nus.edu.sg/event/26-01-23-wing-lab-tour/</link><pubDate>Fri, 23 Jan 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://wing.comp.nus.edu.sg/event/26-01-23-wing-lab-tour/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;AAAI 2026 has been held in Singapore from January 20 to January 27. Some of our group members are excited to travel to the conference site (at Expo) to communicate research. In conjunction with our regular group meeting on Friday, January 23, we are delighted to invite AAAI participants to visit our WING lab and experience the NUS Computing environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;With our visitors, this group meeting had a special agenda:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://yocodeyo.github.io" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;Minzhi Li&lt;/a&gt; from WING NUS gave a presentation to debrief her 2025 internship experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.gesis.org/en/institute/about-us/staff/person/Lu.Gan" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;Dr. Lu Gan&lt;/a&gt; (from &lt;a href="https://www.gesis.org/en/home" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;GESIS - Leibniz Institute for the Social Sciences&lt;/a&gt;) gave a presentation about an AAAI paper from their team, titled &amp;ldquo;GSAP-ERE: Fine-Grained Scholarly Entity and Relation Extraction Focused on Machine Learning&amp;rdquo; (available &lt;a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2511.09411" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Finally, we had a round of self-introductions for all WING members as well as the visitors to socialize and discuss research.&lt;/p&gt;
